><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Practitionersmay obtain value frommonitoringmental fatigue during&#xD;the pre-season phase, especially towards the latter stages where&#xD;mental fatigue may be elevated.&#xD;• Athletes report mental fatigue to be related to ‘readiness to perform’.&#xD;• Salivary markers of sCort and sAA do not appear to be a sensitive or&#xD;robust objective indicator of mental fatigue in the applied sporting&#xD;environment.&#xD;• Practitioners should work to identify and manage mental fatigue experienced&#xD;by players with the same level of importance given to the&#xD;periodisation of physical fatigue.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="0" rect="595.276000,159.130000,779.276000,251.130000"
/></highlight
